# Research Before Implementing
# (canonical version: AGENTS.md)

When you encounter functionality you are not confident about, do NOT implement from scratch immediately.

1. SEARCH WIDELY
   - Code hosting: GitHub, GitLab, Gitea, Codeberg, Bitbucket, SourceForge, AWS CodeConnections (CodeConnect), Gist
   - Registries: npm, PyPI, crates.io, Maven Central, NuGet, Go modules, Packagist, RubyGems, Hex
   - Docs: official docs, RFCs, Awesome lists, Stack Overflow, vendor SDKs

2. EVALUATE EACH CANDIDATE
   - Maintenance: commits < 6 months; issues/PRs answered recently. Skip stale/abandoned regardless of stars.
   - License: clear and compatible. Reject unclear/missing/incompatible.
   - Popularity: stars are unreliable (star-farming). Prefer dependents, downloads, references.
   - Dependencies: count, age, size, known CVEs, transitive risk.
   - Known issues: open bugs, advisories, breaking-change history.
   - Fit: API shape, language/version, platform support.

3. DECIDE
   - Prefer proven designs; adapt, don't copy-paste.
   - Never copy incompatible or unidentifiable code.
   - Compare trade-offs if multiple fit.
   - If nothing fits, explain why, then implement from scratch.

4. REPORT
   Briefly note sources checked, maintenance status, license, and why chosen/rejected.
